# SPA fallback: Pages must serve index.html for unknown paths so deep links to
# /daily, /practice and /leaderboard work (§9.1, AC-036).
#
# `/api/*` deliberately has NO rule here. It belongs to the Worker route
# declared in `wrangler.jsonc` (`acgame.win/api/*`), and a rule of any kind —
# even the self-rewrite `/api/*  /api/:splat  200` that used to sit above this
# line — claims the path for Pages instead. With no matching static asset the
# request then falls through to the SPA fallback below and `/api/providers`
# answers 200 with index.html, which `fetchProviders` parses as JSON and throws
# on: the sign-in dialog loses its Google and Apple buttons.

/*      /index.html  200
